Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
int sum = 0;
System.out.println('Enter numbers (-1 to stop):');
while (sc.hasNextInt()) {
    int n = sc.nextInt();
    if (n == -1) break;
    sum += n;
}
System.out.println('Sum: ' + sum);
sc.close();

Key points: (1) hasNextInt() safely checks before reading — avoids InputMismatchException if non-integer is entered. (2) break on -1 sentinel. (3) Scanner closed after use. Alternatively, read as String and parse, catching NumberFormatException for more robust non-integer handling.

